  "contracts": [
    "CPicture IObject22 is a no-op and its graph is not a proof of embedded resource-reference completeness.",
    "COwnerBitmap+14 is a mode flag; vector frame owning CDraw roots are list+88 node.data8.",
    "Only exact typed CDrawBitmap complete+E4 is a writable member. Cell/Unit child recursion uses the frozen exact class profile.",
    "Named image setter is original CString assignment at self+C, ThisCall void self,CString& ret4. No raw project string writes.",
    "Manager RefreshHashIndex(name,1) invokes original CPicture21, native image encoding/hash and original hash-map refresh. Vector normalization restores its saved root words and RECT on its normal path.",
    "All known unedited resource fields/strings/payloads/raw control bytes remain exact. Changed CString data pointers are adopted only together with an exact native after-string read.",
    "Contained redirect and delete/rename precheck do not claim other animation/dynamic-component/resource references are fully covered.",
    "Second real carrier: CDrawMulBtn full+124 state pointer array -> CImageListInObj+8 frame array -> CImageInObj+68 COwnerBitmap pointer.",
    "Each standard animation pointer is exact-RTTI checked. The thirteen standard animation classes have no COwnerBitmap member; unknown animation/control/provider classes inside the vector tree refuse before mutation.",
    "A named image inside multi-state content is changed by the same original COwnerBitmap slot17, without reinterpreting a frame record or copying opaque payload bytes.",
    "Explicit private-raster replacement selects one full resource image_path, never a global matching-payload owner.",
    "Only direct CDrawBitmap complete+E4 mode0/vector0/frame0 with a nonempty verified cache is accepted for the new branch.",
    "Original slot21 initializes that exact owning image before slot17 sets an existing raster resource name; no raw project flag/string setter is used.",
    "Original CPicture Serialize wraps STORE and LOAD in standalone registration mode1. Persistence is independent embedded pixels, not a permanent nested picture name link."
  ],
